From: OpenWrt
Subject: [PATCH] qca-ssdk: keep the SFP PHY driver bound on later ports

The first I2C-backed SFP PHY device may need a temporary driver binding
released before the QCA SFP driver is registered.  Once that driver has
been registered, however, subsequent SFP PHY devices bind to it directly.
Unconditionally releasing their driver leaves the second SFP port without
a phylib state machine, so PCS link changes never reach the netdev carrier.

Only release an existing binding when it is not the intended QCA SFP
driver.

--- a/src/hsl/phy/sfp_phy.c
+++ b/src/hsl/phy/sfp_phy.c
@@ -680,7 +680,7 @@ int sfp_phy_device_setup(a_uint32_t dev_
 	}
 #if defined(IN_PHY_I2C_MODE)
 	if (hsl_port_phy_access_type_get(dev_id, port) == PHY_I2C_ACCESS) {
-		if(phydev->drv)
+		if(phydev->drv && phydev->drv != &sfp_phy_driver)
 			device_release_driver(&phydev->mdio.dev);
 	}
 #endif
